114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (Undress Code is a Warsaw-based womenswear and lingerie brand founded in 2016, designed in-house and manufactured predominantly in family-owned Polish sewing rooms. Its distribution network spans Harrods, Galeries Lafayette, KaDeWe, Illum Copenhagen, Breuninger, and Revolve. It has been featured in Vogue, Elle, and Women's Health across Europe and Asia. It counts 187,000 followers on Instagram, holds a blue verification badge, and has attracted organic celebrity wear from figures of the scale of Taylor Swift. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 78 0 R
/T (What Undress Code has built)
/E (What Undress Code has built)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (These are not the metrics of a brand that is still finding its footing. They are the metrics of a brand that has arrived at a significant threshold: the moment when a strong product and an instinctive identity must be translated into a communication system that is as intentional as everything else the brand already does.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
117 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (This audit is not a diagnosis of what is missing. It is a reading of where Undress Code is already going, and a proposal for how to get there with more speed and more clarity.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
118 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (The brand's philosophy is anchored in a single statement: made for women who write their own stories. It designs everything in-house in Warsaw, avoids overproduction, eliminates plastic from packaging, and produces with a commitment to quality over volume. Its positioning sits firmly in the premium-to-luxury segment: not accessible mass market, not heritage couture, but the increasingly important middle ground occupied by brands that are serious about craft and serious about relevance.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (The premium independent womenswear and lingerie category is one of the most complex to navigate on Instagram. It requires brands to balance sensuality and sophistication, product specificity and lifestyle aspiration, intimacy and editorial authority. For a brand like Undress Code, which spans lingerie, ready-to-wear, bodysuits, loungewear, and swimwear across a distribution network from Warsaw to Harrods, this tension is amplified: the communication must work simultaneously as product marketing and as world-building. Auditing a brand at this level of complexity, at this stage of its growth, demonstrates the ability to apply analytical rigour to a sector where most assessment remains impressionistic.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
