150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Based on visible interaction data across the reviewed content window, Undress Code's typical feed post registers between 97 and 200 likes, with occasional outliers reaching approximately 1,100/2,200 likes on content that also generates significant shares and comment activity. This pattern is consistent with what the 2026 Socialinsider benchmark data describes for premium fashion accounts in this follower tier: median engagement rates between 0.60% and 1.10%, with significant variance between content types.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The more instructive observation is not the average but the outliers. Posts that significantly exceed the baseline, reaching 1,100 likes with elevated share and comment volume, are the data points that reveal what the audience actually wants to engage with beyond passive consumption.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Identifying the structural characteristics of those posts and building them into a repeatable content logic is where the highest leverage exists.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (Collaborations with content creators consistently outperform brand-produced content on all measurable engagement indicators. This is not unusual: creator content carries the implicit endorsement of a trusted voice and tends to feel more immediate and less constructed than studio-produced imagery. The strategic question it raises is whether the brand is using this performance signal to inform its own content direction, or treating collaborations as a separate track from the main feed.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
