/E (Concretely: one post per week that has the production quality of the editorial register and the human specificity of the immediate register. A carefully shot image of an ordinary moment: a woman adjusting a strap in a public bathroom mirror, sitting in the back of a car at night, waiting for a coffee to cool. The production quality is high. The moment itself is unremarkable. The gap between how carefully the image is made and how ordinary its subject is: that gap is where the Undress Code identity actually lives.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
