1472 0 obj
<<
/Title (This is the strongest caption in the audit window, and the performance confirms it: 1,442 likes on the corresponding lace bra post. It works because it does four things correctly in sequence. It opens with a name that functions as a title, positioning the piece as a character rather than a product. It builds contradiction into the description; delicate but not fragile, soft but not innocent, which is more interesting than a list of qualities. It closes the character description before opening the commercial call to action, so the CTA does not feel like an interruption. And the ellipsis before "Discover new in lingerie now" creates a pause that functions as a breath, separating the editorial register from the commercial one. This caption is a template, not an anomaly. The fact that it is not yet being replicated consistently is the clearest copy gap in the account.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1487 0 R
/Next 1443 0 R
>>
endobj
